WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:17.225
Esther, our costume designer, 
has just been a great addition to the show.

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:19.686
She excelled at this spacesuit.

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:23.314
I pretty much looked at 
every spacesuit there ever was

00:00:23.314 --> 00:00:26.526
both in reality and onscreen.

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:31.489
We were creating a suit
that was feasible, that looked realistic,

00:00:31.573 --> 00:00:36.953
you overlay all the needs of TV,
the specifics that we need—

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:41.124
it becomes a very complicated equation.

00:00:41.416 --> 00:00:42.584
You up for an adventure?

00:00:42.584 --> 00:00:43.877
Only one way to find out.

00:00:46.421 --> 00:00:49.799
One of the biggest requests from Matt and Ben

00:00:49.799 --> 00:00:51.760
was the actual weight of the suit.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:55.096
In Season 3, the suits weighed 70 pounds

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:56.264
It's a lot.

00:00:56.264 --> 00:00:58.975
Our suits are working suits.

00:00:58.975 --> 00:01:03.188
They have to work and they have to look
like they have some function.

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:06.191
I was really happy with the helmet.

00:01:06.191 --> 00:01:08.568
It looks great from all angles,

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.487
and that's a hard one to do.

00:01:11.529 --> 00:01:13.323
Can I get one of those suits?

00:01:13.323 --> 00:01:14.407
They're all booked.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:17.619
This is the only one I got available.

00:01:18.453 --> 00:01:19.913
From the planet Earth-wear

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:22.123
to our Mars habitat,

00:01:22.123 --> 00:01:26.211
we were pushing over 500 fittings on cast.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:29.756
So that's big.
It's a lot of clothes.

00:01:29.839 --> 00:01:32.175
We need to get this thing done.

00:01:32.175 --> 00:01:33.218
This asteroid,

00:01:33.218 --> 00:01:36.596
it could change everything
for people back home.

00:01:36.971 --> 00:01:38.932
The challenge for me was

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:40.517
to sort of set up the dynamics

00:01:40.517 --> 00:01:42.977
that were within the written script.

00:01:43.061 --> 00:01:48.108
We're seeing certainly a lot more color
in our professional crew.

00:01:48.191 --> 00:01:50.985
And then when we look at the Helios crew,

00:01:50.985 --> 00:01:54.280
there's much more utilitarian look about them

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.366
and I think it served the script very well.

00:01:56.449 --> 00:02:00.286
We spent the time and the energy
investigating all of our choices

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:03.581
and making sure
they were the right choices.

00:02:03.665 --> 00:02:06.251
I need skilled people on my side

00:02:06.251 --> 00:02:08.211
and you are very skilled indeed.

